+# Proof outline — S5-CLM-00003489
+
+The frozen hypothesis says that the theorems of `KT` are exactly the source
+boxdot translations provable in a normal logic `L`. The goal is to prove that
+every theorem of `L` is a theorem of `KT`.
+
+1. `toFoundation` and `fromFoundation` give a structural bijection between the
+   source formula type and Foundation's modal formulas over `Nat`. Induction on
+   source derivations sends K and KT proofs forward. The reverse direction
+   recurses over Foundation's Hilbert derivations; explicit substitution lemmas
+   instantiate the K- and T-schemata without strengthening the source record.
+2. `tFoundation` models the source translation. Structural induction proves
+   `toFoundation (t φ) = tFoundation (toFoundation φ)`. A second induction
+   proves that Foundation's proposition-first boxdot translation is K-equivalent
+   to `tFoundation`; conjunction commutativity resolves the box-case ordering.
